  "id": "9412190e-0a34-436f-8410-55a0bfc18ac0",
  "title": "FSSAI Takes Action Against Nestle and HUL Over Misleading Food Claims",
  "summary": "The Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI) has taken legal action against Nestle India and Hindustan Unilever Ltd over misleading claims on their infant food products and packaging. The regulator highlighted issues with promotional language, such as 'no added sugar' and 'healthy muscles', which were found to be non-compliant with food safety regulations.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "FSSAI has issued notices to Nestle India and Hindustan Unilever Ltd for misleading claims on their infant food products.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The FSSAI examined three infant nutrition products and their promotional materials, highlighting issues related to biotin content and promotional language.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Claims such as 'Nutrition for Strong Bones', 'Clinically Proven to Help Improve Bone Strength in 6 Months' and 'Improves Bone Health' were found to be misleading or non-compliant with applicable regulations.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
