      "title": "Nestle, HUL face FSSAI action over inconsistent, misleading labels",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/nestle-hul-face-fssai-action-over-inconsistent-misleading-labels-126101701044_1.html",
      "description": "The food regulator flagged a \"Flavoured Milk\" vs \"Proprietary Food\" mismatch on Nescafe drinks, and bone-health and \"no added sugar\" claims on Horlicks",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-17T18:09:14"
    },
    {
      "title": "FSSAI issues notices to Nestle, HUL over misleading food product claims",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/fssai-issues-notices-to-nestle-hul-over-misleading-food-product-claims-126101700903_1.html",
      "description": "Food regulator FSSAI has issued notices to Nestle India and Hindustan Unilever Ltd for misleading claims on the packaging of some of their food products.\nIn a social media post on Saturday, the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India said notices have been issued against these two companies \"regarding misleading claims and non-compliances\".\nIn the case of HUL, the notice has been issued for misleading claims on its product 'Horlicks Women's Plus Chocolate Nutrition Drink 400g'.\n\"Claims such as 'Nutrition for Strong Bones', 'Clinically Proven to Help Improve Bone Strength in 6 Months' and 'Improves Bone Health' were found to be misleading or non-compliant with applicable regulations,\" FSSAI said.\nThe claim 'healthy Muscles' was found to be in contravention of the provisions governing the use of the term \"healthy\" in food claims.\nApart from that, the claim \"No Added Sugar\" was considered misleading in view of the presence of maltodextrin in the product, the regulator pointed ..",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-17T16:13:56"
    }
  ]
